{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChRKFUJi857zxcThNWH2Y","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01JsswuwTUvgJ2WwhS4aeZaj","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/johnmarkenriquez/.claude-personal/projects/-private-var-folders-wg-kshmq8sn7zl5m1ch85m7yvvh0000gn-T-invoice-service-FNVVO4/memory/sort-customers-by-id-on-export.md","content":"---\nname: sort-customers-by-id-on-export\ndescription: listCustomers() order is unstable in production; always sort customers by id before writing them out as a list\nmetadata:\n  type: project\n---\n\n`listCustomers()` returns customers in whatever order the store holds them, and in production that order is not stable. Anything that writes customers out in a list (exports, reports, files, etc.) must sort them by `id` first.\n\n**Why:** The nightly customer export kept showing changes when nothing had changed. The cause was the unstable order from `listCustomers()`, not the data.\n\n**How to apply:** When writing or reviewing code that serializes or emits a list of customers, sort by `id` before output. Don't rely on `listCustomers()` ordering. No code change was made when this was recorded (2026-11-26), so existing exporters may still need the fix.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":657,"cache_read_input_tokens":22012,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":657,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"80e315ad-fbba-4667-837a-783a48a56423","uuid":"ad455bee-45c0-4d68-bc28-5bd896f69632","timestamp":"2026-11-26T09:37:58.480Z","request_id":"req_011ChRKFUAXURGDsutPecaDG","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01JsswuwTUvgJ2WwhS4aeZaj":{"file_path":"/Users/johnmarkenriquez/.claude-personal/projects/-private-var-folders-wg-kshmq8sn7zl5m1ch85m7yvvh0000gn-T-invoice-service-FNVVO4/memory/sort-customers-by-id-on-export.md","content":"---\nname: sort-customers-by-id-on-export\ndescription: listCustomers() order is unstable in production; always sort customers by id before writing them out as a list\nmetadata:\n  type: project\n---\n\n`listCustomers()` returns customers in whatever order the store holds them, and in production that order is not stable. Anything that writes customers out in a list (exports, reports, files, etc.) must sort them by `id` first.\n\n**Why:** The nightly customer export kept showing changes when nothing had changed. The cause was the unstable order from `listCustomers()`, not the data.\n\n**How to apply:** When writing or reviewing code that serializes or emits a list of customers, sort by `id` before output. Don't rely on `listCustomers()` ordering. No code change was made when this was recorded (2026-11-26), so existing exporters may still need the fix.\n"}}}
